  "style": "Write gender-neutral Hebrew: use nouns of action for commands and buttons (פתיחה, שמירה, ביטול) and the infinitive or plural forms in instructions, never masculine-only imperatives. Hebrew has no capitalisation; keep labels short and without niqqud. Use the single ellipsis character … after a label that opens a dialog, and the ordinary Hebrew punctuation (, . : ?) with the maqaf - in compounds such as תלת-ממד. Latin do-not-translate tokens, numbers, coordinates and key names (Ctrl, Shift, Alt) stay unchanged and left-to-right; isolate them (FSI/PDI or <bdi>) inside Hebrew text. Write menu paths in reading order with \" ◂ \" (for example קובץ ◂ פתיחה) because ▸ is not mirrored in right-to-left text."
